@startuml
title Current E2EE device-level realtime flow

actor DeviceA
actor DeviceB
participant "STOMP /ws" as WS
participant "StompAuthInterceptor" as AUTH
participant "StompConnectionRegistry" as REG
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Simple Broker" as BROKER

DeviceA -> WS: CONNECT Authorization: Bearer JWT
WS -> AUTH: CONNECT
AUTH -> DB: validate persisted session + bound ACTIVE device
DB --> AUTH: valid session + device
AUTH --> WS: StompDevicePrincipal
AUTH -> REG: link connection to server session

DeviceA -> WS: SUBSCRIBE /topic/devices/{ownDeviceId}
WS -> AUTH: exact-match + liveness revalidation
AUTH -> DB: session + device ACTIVE check
DB --> AUTH: live
AUTH --> WS: subscription allowed

DeviceB -> WS: CONNECT Authorization: Bearer JWT
WS -> AUTH: CONNECT
AUTH -> DB: validate persisted session + bound ACTIVE device
DB --> AUTH: valid session + device
AUTH --> WS: StompDevicePrincipal
AUTH -> REG: link connection to server session
DeviceB -> WS: SUBSCRIBE /topic/devices/{ownDeviceId}
WS -> AUTH: exact-match + liveness revalidation
AUTH --> WS: subscription allowed

note over AUTH
Any other destination is rejected identically.
There is no client SEND handler.
end note

note over REG
Session or device revocation terminates
live connections server-side.
end note
@enduml
